  "verbalization": "Phenazopyridine appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving the Scn10a protein, as evidenced by its binding to multiple SCN family members—Scn7a, Scn11a, and Scn8a—each of which participates in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This suggests that Phenazopyridine may modulate sodium channel function by targeting a common pathway, potentially influencing the activity of Scn10a. The consistent involvement of Scn10a in the voltage-gated sodium channel activity, as indicated by the final scores in the paths, implies a functional link between Phenazopyridine and Scn10a. The overlapping roles of these SCN proteins in sodium channel regulation suggest that Phenazopyridine may exert its effects through a shared regulatory mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of these channels in a broader cellular context. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Phenazopyridine to influence sodium channel function, which could have implications for neuronal activity and related physiological processes.",
